{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.regex.Matcher;\nimport java.util.regex.Pattern;\n\npublic class CF_723B {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        Matcher m = Pattern.compile(\"\\\\([a-zA-Z_]*\\\\)\").matcher(s);\n        StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer();\n        while (m.find()) {\n            m.appendReplacement(sb, \"_\");\n        }\n        m.appendTail(sb);\n        String replaced = sb.toString();\n\n        int maxLen = Pattern.compile(\"_+\").splitAsStream(replaced)\n                .mapToInt(String::length)\n                .max()\n                .orElse(0);\n        System.out.println(maxLen);\n\n        System.out.println(countWordsInParentheses(s));\n    }\n\n    static int countWordsInParentheses(String s) {\n        int words = 0;\n        boolean open = false;\n        int start = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n            char c = s.charAt(i);\n            if (c == '(') {\n                open = true;\n                start = i;\n            } else if (open && c == ')') {\n                open = false;\n                words += countWords(s.substring(start + 1, i));\n            }\n        }\n        return words;\n    }\n\n    static int countWords(String text) {\n        if (text.isEmpty()) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        return (int) Pattern.compile(\"_+\").splitAsStream(text)\n                .filter(word -> !word.isEmpty())\n                .count();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport re\nimport sys\n\ndef count_words(text: str) -> int:\n    if not text:\n        return 0\n    parts = re.split(r'_+', text)\n    return sum(1 for p in parts if p)\n\ndef count_words_in_parentheses(s: str) -> int:\n    words = 0\n    open_flag = False\n    start = -1\n    for i, c in enumerate(s):\n        if c == '(':\n            open_flag = True\n            start = i\n        elif open_flag and c == ')':\n            open_flag = False\n            words += count_words(s[start+1:i])\n    return words\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1] if len(data) > 1 else ''\n    \n    # Replace parenthesized groups with a single underscore\n    replaced = re.sub(r'\\([a-zA-Z_]*\\)', '_', s)\n    \n    # Split by underscores and find max length of parts\n    parts = re.split(r'_+', replaced)\n    max_len = max((len(p) for p in parts), default=0)\n    print(max_len)\n    \n    # Count words inside parentheses\n    print(count_words_in_parentheses(s))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.602820692729438e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.3947389561508317e-05, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -0.2519339621067047, -0.38697919249534607, -1.9311717551317997e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.099436753473128